  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/characters.js",
   "l": 12,
   "t": "Daughter of the Keeper of Lanternfall. Reads every book the tide brings in. Wants, more than anything, to leave."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/characters.js",
   "l": 20,
   "t": "Wren's best friend since before either could walk. Herbalist's apprentice. Has a plan for everything, including the plan"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/characters.js",
   "l": 28,
   "t": "Squire of the Dawnguard, exiled to Lanternfall after he froze during his knighting trial. Loud. Kind. Certain he is a co"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/characters.js",
   "l": 36,
   "t": "Washed ashore in a storm with no memory and a Crest no Lantern has ever seen."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/characters.js",
   "l": 44,
   "t": "Aurenne street kid. Steals for a living, lies for fun, and would die before admitting he's eleven."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/characters.js",
   "l": 52,
   "t": "Captain of the airship Halcyon. Smuggler, gambler, Dawnguard deserter. Owes everyone money, including himself."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 8,
   "t": "Lemonade (with mint)"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 8,
   "t": "s lemonade, for Bess. It has been on its way for forty years."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 72,
   "t": "A splinter of the broken sun that learned to walk. It is warm, and it is not kind."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 77,
   "t": "The Choir's hounds, bred in the Spire's light. They cast no shadow at all."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 82,
   "t": "An eye of noon, floating. Looking at it is like looking at the sun, which nobody has done for a year."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 84,
   "t": "Vesper Lancer"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 87,
   "t": "The Spire's guard. They have been promised the best day of their lives, as soon as their shift ends."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 89,
   "t": "Choir Seraph"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 92,
   "t": "A hymn given wings. It heals whatever stands between it and you."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 97,
   "t": "Keeper of the Spire's back door. He has turned away four hundred pilgrims and remembers every face."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 101,
   "t": "Hour Knight"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 104,
   "t": "Armor wound like a clock. It stops when it is struck — and so, for a moment, do you."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 109,
   "t": "A moment that never ended, drifting. Cold as an afternoon that will not let you go home."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 111,
   "t": "Memory Moth"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 114,
   "t": "They eat memories the way other moths eat coats. The Spire is a feast."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 119,
   "t": "They practice the Vespersong in shifts. Somebody, somewhere in the Spire, is always singing it."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 121,
   "t": "The Hour-Warden"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 124,
   "t": "The Spire's keeper of hours. It has only ever counted to twelve, and it has done so for forty years."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 128,
   "t": "Festival Puppet"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 131,
   "t": "\"Lovely day for it!\" it says, and smiles, and smiles, and comes for your throat."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 133,
   "t": "Paper Lantern"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 136,
   "t": "A festival lantern that drifted loose. The candle inside has burned for forty years and never got any shorter."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 138,
   "t": "Gilded Hound"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 141,
   "t": "Somebody's dog, remembered as a very good dog. Remembered a little too hard."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 146,
   "t": "\"Welcome to the Festival of the Long Light. Enjoy the day.\" Forever."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 148,
   "t": "Maypole Dancer"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 151,
   "t": "She has been dancing round the maypole since before your parents were born. She would love you to join in."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 153,
   "t": "Choir of the Dead"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 156,
   "t": "Mercy's congregation. They sing for her because she promised them they would never have to stop."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 161,
   "t": "Evernoon's warden. She believes that a day which never ends cannot hurt anyone. She has never once been told no and beli"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 168,
   "t": "Where Evernoon comes apart, the Gloam comes in. It wears whatever it finds."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 170,
   "t": "Frayed Puppet"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 173,
   "t": "Its strings are cut. Its sentence is unfinished. It is very, very angry about both."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 175,
   "t": "What the Noon Forgot"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 178,
   "t": "Every sentence Evernoon never finished, knotted together into something that wants, very badly, to be heard."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 218,
   "t": "\"Lovely day for—\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 218,
   "t": "\"Any moment n—\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 218,
   "t": "\"Ask me—\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 218,
   "t": "\"Look how high it g—\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 218,
   "t": "\"Have you seen my Lys—\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 226,
   "t": "The Warden's clock-face cracks — its hands spin all the way back!"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 231,
   "t": "TWELVE. The Hour-Warden strikes noon."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 234,
   "t": "s hand moves. It is ${HOURS[c.m.hour]} o"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 241,
   "t": "\"NOON.\" Every bell in Evernoon rings at once."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 242,
   "t": "\"Sing with me, children.\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 244,
   "t": "Mercy lets down her hood. \"You will not take her. You will not take ANY of them.\" She sings the Vespersong."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 249,
   "t": "Hush. Be still. Be still forever.\""
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 250,
   "t": "\"Rest now.\" A lullaby — and under it, the bells of Evernoon begin to swing..."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 256,
   "t": "\"—IT!\" A hundred mouths finish the sentence at once."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 258,
   "t": "It begins to forget its own shape. Light pours through the gaps — light no longer heals it!"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch10.js",
   "l": 268,
   "t": "A puppet tears loose from its body and staggers forward!"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch11.js",
   "l": 14,
   "t": "Starfall Fragment"
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch11.js",
   "l": 15,
   "t": "s cutlass, from the wreck of the Gull's Return. Still sharp. He oiled it every Sunday."
  },
  {
   "f": "src/data/content/ch11.js",
